id: pm-ciadvisoryreceipt
title: Retain dependency advisory failure evidence in CI
description: "Required static jobs119465264554 and119475057456 stop at the dependency advisory collector without retaining .cache/dependency-security/receipt.json. GitHub artifacts omit the per-feed result, so the operator cannot distinguish unavailable feeds from positive advisories. Fresh local registry and OSV collection at20:43UTC completes with zero positives. Preserve the existing closed collector implementation and add CI evidence retention to diagnose the hosted blocker precisely."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,review-feedback,security
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:50:42.159Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T22:07:12.201Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T22:07:11.000Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T22:07:11.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: Retain the explicit advisory receipt on both successful and failed static jobs; Scope hidden-file upload to the single inspected public receipt and distinguish rerun attempts; Preserve strict gate outcomes and prove the workflow retention contract
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: low
confidence: 90
resolution: Keep the bounded static-only always-run advisory upload and strengthen its ordering regression to require a present lint step before comparing upload positions. Version the existing review-contract recurrence family for this captured missing-step counterexample.
expected_result: "Failed static jobs retain inspectable original feed evidence, and the regression cannot silently accept a missing lint boundary."
actual_result: The hosted failed receipt retained and identified both real Vitest advisories. The missing-lint counterexample admits under the old comparison and is refused by the new explicit existence precondition. All22 linked workflow cases and lint pass; final-head required CI remains mandatory before merge.
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
