comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:50:42.159Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: full all-status intake and live advisory searches found closed pm-eqxjzl for collector freshness and completeness but no CI failure-artifact owner. Reuse the security capability and recorded scanner import lineage. This item fixes missing hosted diagnostics and does not assert an unverified vulnerability or weaken the advisory gate."
  "2026-10-21T20:54:15.213Z","harness:codex","Evidence: hosted required static jobs https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/39669768351/job/119465264554 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/39669768351/job/119475057456 both refuse in the advisory collector. Neither attempt retains its receipt, so the actual hosted feed failure is unknown. Independent local collection at20:43UTC completes registry and OSV with zero positives; this does not establish hosted feed availability. The existing collector stores only public package/version/advisory IDs, input hashes, counts and timestamps, with no raw command stderr or credentials. Upload is limited to its exact receipt file, not the containing cache."
  "2026-10-21T20:54:16.019Z","harness:codex","Regression sensitivity: the unchanged new workflow contract fails before the retention step because it finds zero matching uploads. After the change all22 CI workflow contract cases pass. The new contract evaluates successful and failed static executions plus all other gate variants, checks hidden-file inclusion, bounds upload to the single receipt, and separates run attempts. Type checking, focused ESLint and read-only workflow-permission verification pass. Strict advisory verdicts and collection behavior are unchanged; hosted receipt and gate verification remain merge prerequisites."
  "2026-10-21T21:12:44.982Z","harness:codex","Hosted validation: artifact dependency-advisory-39674740199-1 now retains the original complete receipt after a failed static gate. OSV reports GHSA-qxg6-89mg-rqv8 and GHSA-xp26-3454-mjgp for @vitest/mocker4.1.11 across all569 locked versions; registry counts are zero. The collector is correctly refusing positive advisories, not suffering a feed outage. Its new retention behavior is verified; remediation is tracked individually under pm-vitest4112."
  "2026-10-21T22:06:06.133Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit inline4342443158 identifies a valid ordering-test gap: without a lint step findIndex returns-1 and uploadIndex>-1 still passes. Reopen the canonical retention issue for the focused assertion repair; require a present lint step before comparing positions. This changes the test contract, not collector behavior or CI admission policy."
  "2026-10-21T22:07:09.735Z","harness:codex","Review fix: name the lint index, require it to be nonnegative, and only then assert upload ordering. A counterexample made from the parsed real workflow confirms the former comparison accepts missing lint and the new existence precondition refuses it. The full linked workflow file passes22/22 after the fix, lint passes, and the scanner control remains unchanged."
